<title>CHINA: China's Henan sets summer wheat output record.</title>
<headline>China's Henan sets summer wheat output record.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central China's Henan province produced a record 7.3 million tonnes of wheat this summer, up by 22 percent compared with last year, the Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The province grew wheat on 1.53 million hectares of land, it said.</p>
<p>Henan now has 13,333 hectares of high-yield non-irrigated land, with per hectare yield reaching 6-7.5 tonnes of wheat, it said.</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
